{
  "id": "icmp",
  "label": "ICMP",
  "rfc": ["792"],
  "notes": "ICMP over IPv4 (protocol 1). All fields of the 8-byte common header are modelled. The four bytes after the checksum are modelled at their fixed offsets as Identifier and Sequence Number; for other message types those bytes carry type-specific data (gateway, pointer, and so on) that is not modelled. ICMPv6 (RFC 4443) is a different protocol and is not covered by this entry. The Code field is kept as a number because its meaning depends on Type.",
